{
 "id": "AT-SW-02 (settings writer: every refusal writes nothing)",
 "owner": "core",
 "note": "0.1.2 settings writer: refused calls exit 3, write nothing and leave no backup. The six consent keys are refused on every path (set and reset, dry run and --apply, beside a valid key), since the helper cannot tell a user's ! line from a model's call; the refusal names the user-run ways (/config, the file by hand, and for a value the plugin reads Claude Code's own `claude plugin configure <plugin>@<marketplace> --values-stdin`). A value the plugin would not read as written (type, min and max, enum values, a whole number, the window floor, a relative path or one with a space at an end, a control character, a value over 4096 bytes, a list over 32 entries, a number from 1e15 or one that prints in e-notation, each pattern list's own rules: a deny class name, a NAME glob with a /) is refused with the reason, never with a pattern's text. A protective list only gains entries and resume_proceed only goes towards confirm (a removal that loosens nothing still goes). Files refused: not plain JSON, a non-object on the path, a member named twice, two keys for the plugin, no entry and no marketplace known, an @inline run, another CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, a hard link, no file (a reset then has nothing to remove), a folder.",
 "now": "2026-10-30T09:00:00+02:00",
 "tz": "Etc/GMT-2",
